<title>USA: Rubin - supports move to change IRS farm tax rule.</title>
<headline>Rubin - supports move to change IRS farm tax rule.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said Monday that he would support legislation in Congress to overturn an IRS ruling that bars farmers from using commodity contracts to defer income into the next tax year.</p>
<p>In a letter to members of Congress, Rubin said that while Treasury tax advisers said the IRS ruling &quot;correctly interprets the current law,&quot; he would support efforts on Capitol Hill to rewrite the law.</p>
<p>Twenty-nine senators -- including Republican leader Trent Lott of Mississippi and Democratic leader Tom Daschle of South Dakota -- have agreed to cosponsor the legislation.</p>
</text>
